cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "US Immigration Data — open datasets on US immigration procedure and enforcement"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable time series and reference datasets on United States immigration
  procedure and enforcement. Government sources publish only the current version of most
  of this information and overwrite it without notice; these datasets bank each observed
  change, so the history — what changed, when, and whom it affected — remains available
  after the official page no longer shows it. Contents include TPS designation history
  (1994–2026), USCIS fee history across 40 forms, month-over-month Visa Bulletin
  movement, 287(g) agreements with per-agency signing dates, banked ICE detention
  population snapshots, DOJ-recognized legal-aid provision by immigration court, and a
  verified change log. Every value cites its official source inside the file.
type: dataset
message: "If you use these datasets, please cite them as below."
authors:
  - name: "MigrantUSA Editorial"
    website: "https://migrantusa.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/migrantusa/us-immigration-data"
url: "https://migrantusa.com/datasets/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - immigration
  - United States
  - temporary protected status
  - USCIS
  - visa bulletin
  - immigration enforcement
  - 287(g)
  - immigration detention
  - immigration court
  - open data
